  "methods": {
    "plugin_system": "yes / no / partial from the pinned tree's docs. own-team optional modules and independently maintained modules; not found when no source.",
    "blvm_size": "Default node first-party crates plus blvm-sdk (blvm-storage-fence lives in the node tree; blvm-sdk-macros lives in the sdk tree). blvm-spec-lock non-test lines are tooling. Tests include spec-lock tests. Same tokei 14 and #[cfg(test)] rules as test_split.",
    "test_split": "tokei 14 code lines in programming languages only. A file under tests/, test/, e2e/, qa/, or functional/, or named *_test/_tests/test_*, counts as tests. Rust lines inside a #[cfg(test)] or #[cfg(all(..., test))] item count as tests. Partition: fuzz paths (fuzz/, fuzz_targets/, src/test/fuzz/); property (path or name contains property/proptest/quickcheck/hypothesis/orange_paper_property); C++ src/test as unit; remaining integration dirs as integration; other in-source tests as unit. Benches under bench(es)/ are grouped with unit. Vendored and locale paths are excluded.",
    "fuzz_targets": "Count of cargo-fuzz targets in fuzz/fuzz_targets/*.rs (excluding mod.rs) plus Bitcoin Core-style src/test/fuzz/*.cpp (excluding util helpers). Measured at the pinned checkout.",
    "vector_files": "Files whose path or name looks like a test vector (vector, tx_valid, tx_invalid, script_tests, sighash, bipN) with suffix .json, .csv, or .hex.",
    "spec_files": "Documentation or model files whose name looks like a spec (spec, THE_ORANGE_PAPER, orange paper, bipN) with suffix .md, .rst, .txt, .lean, or .tex. LICENSE and contributing files are excluded."
  },
